{"availability":"available","full":"Arthur031221/Sunspill","name":"Sunspill","description":"Set up your own room on a phone, then see where the sun lands on its floor by the hour and the season. Buildings from OpenStreetMap, a check against the sun you saw. Your room stays in the browser.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T10:25:31Z","updated":"2026-10-11T12:35:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://arthur031221.github.io/Sunspill/","topics":["canvas","floor-plan","interior-design","javascript","mobile-first","openstreetmap","pwa","shadow","solar","sun-position","sunlight","visualization","web-app","window"],"demo":"https://arthur031221.github.io/Sunspill/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:56.762Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:56.762Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:56.762Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:50:56.762Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Set up your own room in a few minutes, then see where the sun lands on its floor, by the hour and the season.","English | zh-TW | zh-CN | ja | ko | es | fr | de | pt-BR","Made for a phone. Seven steps and a few minutes get you from an address to your own room. Your room stays in your browser. The last one you edited is kept on your device, along with any you name and save. Address search, the map and building outlines ask public OpenStreetMap servers, and only after you say yes to each one."],"features":["Draw the room. Size, wall thickness, up to four windows with a shade, a balcony and a rail, up to three doors, the floor number and furniture you can turn.","Scrub any day. Pick a city, an address, your location or a latitude and longitude. The clock, the sun path and the patch follow, and daylight saving is handled.","Check the afternoon. A printed rule: the minutes after a time you choose when direct sun reaches the floor or a wall, averaged o